    "wm-id": 804670,
    "content": {
      "html": "<p><i>In reply to <a class=\"u-in-reply-to\" href=\"https://hacdias.com/articles/2020/05/back-90s/\">https://hacdias.com/articles/2020/05/back-90s/</a>.</i></p>\n<p>Love the animated GIFs! The background!</p>\n<p>One thing: my feed reader has a hard time handling the relative image URLs in your RSS … (Hint: <a href=\"https://validator.w3.org/feed/docs/warning/ContainsRelRef.html\">https://validator.w3.org/feed/docs/warning/ContainsRelRef.html</a>. [I only know about this link because I ran into the same thing —different blog, though—earlier this week.])</p>\n<p>(Also, I couldn’t help but notice that RSS items lack the “context” that makes replies and such so much more understandable. Not a huge issue, just thought I’d let you know.)</p>",
      "text": "In reply to https://hacdias.com/articles/2020/05/back-90s/.\nLove the animated GIFs! The background!\nOne thing: my feed reader has a hard time handling the relative image URLs in your RSS … (Hint: https://validator.w3.org/feed/docs/warning/ContainsRelRef.html. [I only know about this link because I ran into the same thing —different blog, though—earlier this week.])\n(Also, I couldn’t help but notice that RSS items lack the “context” that makes replies and such so much more understandable. Not a huge issue, just thought I’d let you know.)"
    },
